 "semantics": "Three lines: n (1<=n<=10^5); n integers 0<=a_i<=10^4; one string s_0..s_{n-1} of exactly n binary digits, m = sum 2^i*s_i (s_0 is the least significant bit, trailing zeros of s are leading zeros of m). Output max over 0<=x<=m of f(x) = sum of a_i over set bits i of x, as one integer (<=10^9). Since a_i>=0, the optimum is x=m or, for some set bit i of m, clear bit i, keep every higher set bit and set every lower bit: prefix(a_0..a_{i-1}) + sum of a_j over set bits j>i. Unique integer output; cross-checked against direct enumeration of every x in [0, m] and an independent tight/free bit DP.",
 "sourceCorrectionProposal": {
  "description": [
   [
    "from 0 to 2n - 1 as",
    "from 0 to 2<sup>n</sup> - 1 as",
    1
   ],
   [
    "(11 = 20 + 21 + 23)",
    "(11 = 2<sup>0</sup> + 2<sup>1</sup> + 2<sup>3</sup>)",
    1
